@title Booking web tier architecture
@subtitle Calloway Travel, region eu-west-1
@author Booking Platform
@date 2026-09-28
@width wide

## Overview

Customers reach us through CloudFront, with a WAF in front. The tier is spread over two Availability Zones so it survives losing one.

## Diagram

diagram web dir=LR title="Booking web tier, eu-west-1"
web: travelers "Travelers" user
web: cdn "CloudFront and WAF" ext
web: partner "Partner Inventory API" ext
web: alb "Application Load Balancer" lb focus
web: nata "NAT Gateway A" svc
web: natb "NAT Gateway B" svc
web: weba "Web Fleet A" svc "Auto Scaling group"
web: webb "Web Fleet B" svc "Auto Scaling group"
web: dbp "Bookings DB Primary" db focus
web: dbs "Bookings DB Standby" db
web: s3ep "S3 Gateway Endpoint" store
web: group public "Public subnets 10.40.0.0/23" alb, nata, natb
web: group app "App subnets 10.40.10.0/23" weba, webb
web: group data "Data subnets 10.40.20.0/23" dbp, dbs
web: group vpc "Booking VPC 10.40.0.0/16" public, app, data, s3ep
web: group acct "Booking account" vpc
web: travelers -> cdn : HTTPS
web: cdn -> alb : origin request
web: alb -> weba, webb : port 8080
web: weba -> dbp : SQL
web: webb -> dbp : SQL
web: dbp -> dbs : synchronous replication
web: weba -> nata : outbound
web: nata -> partner : HTTPS
web: webb -> s3ep : receipts

## Capacity

table = component,size,scaling; Web fleets,m6i.large,3 to 12 instances per AZ on CPU above 55%; Bookings DB,db.r6g.2xlarge Multi-AZ,Storage autoscaling to 4 TB; NAT gateways,One per AZ,5 Gbps each
